findings.message:
DoS Vulnerability Identified.

VULNERABILITY: Unrestricted Toggling of Refund State in finalize Function
'''
The `finalize()` function can be called by anyone after the funding deadline (block.number > fundingEndBlock + 8*oneweek). It sets `funding = false` and toggles `refundstate`. Since there is no access control on this function (except the conditional ether send to owner), any external user can repeatedly call `finalize()` to flip `refundstate` between true and false at will. This allows an attacker to disable the refund mechanism precisely when legitimate users attempt to claim refunds via `refundTRA()`, thereby causing a Denial of Service for the refund functionality.

**Mitigation:** Ensure `finalize()` can only be called once, or restrict its invocation to the contract owner. For example, add a boolean flag `finalized` that prevents multiple calls:
```
bool public finalized = false;
function finalize() external {
    if (block.number <= fundingEndBlock + 8*oneweek) throw;
    if (finalized) throw;
    finalized = true;
    funding = false;
    refundstate = true; // Set to true permanently (or as intended)
    if (msg.sender == owner) {
        owner.send(this.balance);
    }
}
```
Alternatively, separate the refund activation from finalization to prevent unauthorized toggling.
```
Detector: DoSDetector
Classification: SWC-113 / SWC-128, DASP-5
